1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,740
One in five hundred people has this disease.

2
00:00:03,040 --> 00:00:08,930
A test catches ninety-nine percent of the sick and wrongly flags one percent of the healthy.

3
00:00:09,230 --> 00:00:12,290
If yours says positive, what's the chance you're sick?

4
00:00:12,590 --> 00:00:13,560
Pick a number.

5
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:22,350
At one Boston-area hospital, most doctors and medical students given a problem like this got it wrong.

6
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:27,900
Their most common answer was their test's own accuracy: ninety-five percent.

7
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:32,080
For our test, that's ninety-nine: you'd start treatment today.

8
00:00:32,533 --> 00:00:36,773
Check that rule by counting: ten thousand people, half of them sick.

9
00:00:37,233 --> 00:00:39,653
Test everyone, and watch who lights up.

10
00:00:40,700 --> 00:00:44,630
Of the five thousand who lit up, ninety-nine percent are sick.

11
00:00:44,930 --> 00:00:46,410
Here, the rule holds.

12
00:00:46,866 --> 00:00:53,396
Now keep the same test, and make the disease rarer and rarer, down to yours: one in five hundred.

13
00:00:54,233 --> 00:00:59,773
About twenty sick people light up, plus one percent of everyone else: about a hundred.

14
00:01:00,366 --> 00:01:03,956
So of a hundred twenty positives, only twenty are sick.

15
00:01:04,166 --> 00:01:05,656
Seventeen percent.

16
00:01:06,800 --> 00:01:08,530
The rule said ninety-nine.

17
00:01:08,730 --> 00:01:10,310
Six times too high.

18
00:01:11,300 --> 00:01:16,010
One percent sounds small, but here it's one percent of nearly everyone.

19
00:01:16,466 --> 00:01:21,016
Your positive result ruled out everyone who tested negative.

20
00:01:21,633 --> 00:01:26,433
What's left is a smaller sample space: these hundred twenty people.

21
00:01:26,900 --> 00:01:30,740
Your chance of being sick is the red share of this crowd.

22
00:01:31,040 --> 00:01:33,810
Twenty, out of twenty plus a hundred.

23
00:01:35,333 --> 00:01:44,243
Unrounded, the red count is twenty sick people times ninety-nine percent, and the blue, every healthy person times one percent.

24
00:01:44,833 --> 00:01:48,733
Divide everything by ten thousand: counts become shares.

25
00:01:49,133 --> 00:01:50,663
The share stays the same.

26
00:01:51,100 --> 00:01:56,330
These are how common each group is, and these are how often each group tests positive.

27
00:01:56,630 --> 00:01:58,840
Name them, and you have Bayes' theorem.

28
00:01:59,300 --> 00:02:04,590
All it does is shrink the sample space to what the evidence allows, then take the share.

29
00:02:05,933 --> 00:02:08,413
Swap the disease for a police watch list.

30
00:02:08,866 --> 00:02:15,946
For the twenty seventeen Champions League final, about a hundred seventy thousand people came to Cardiff.

31
00:02:16,346 --> 00:02:23,926
The watch lists held about twelve hundred photos, so even a small error rate per face would swamp the real matches.

32
00:02:24,366 --> 00:02:27,126
Face-recognition cameras scanned the crowds.

33
00:02:27,426 --> 00:02:31,646
Over four days, they raised two thousand four hundred seventy alerts.

34
00:02:32,033 --> 00:02:33,393
Shrink to the alerts.

35
00:02:33,793 --> 00:02:34,973
Take the red share.

36
00:02:35,313 --> 00:02:39,823
The police counted a hundred seventy-three as right: seven percent.

37
00:02:40,433 --> 00:02:43,493
In machine learning, that share is called precision.

38
00:02:44,733 --> 00:02:51,153
Cardiff University's evaluators counted only alerts the logbooks confirmed: three percent.

39
00:02:51,653 --> 00:03:04,063
Months later, a new algorithm, better photos and practised operators thinned out the false alarms, the blue term in Bayes' denominator, and their count rose to forty-six percent.

40
00:03:04,666 --> 00:03:05,886
Back to your test.

41
00:03:08,013 --> 00:03:11,243
Your seventeen percent assumes a random screen.

42
00:03:11,643 --> 00:03:20,243
Symptoms raise the one in five hundred: at one in a hundred, fifty percent; at one in two, ninety-nine, where the rule held.

43
00:03:22,266 --> 00:03:28,086
The title's ninety-nine percent is the test's recall: how often the sick test positive.

44
00:03:28,386 --> 00:03:33,206
Seventeen percent is its precision: how often the positive are sick.

